@startuml
title Booking.com — репликация критичных PostgreSQL-кластеров
 left to right direction
 skinparam componentStyle rectangle
 skinparam shadowing false
 skinparam defaultFontSize 12

 component "Booking / Inventory / Payment\nservices" as App #FFE4B5
 rectangle "Routing layer" as Routing {
   component "HA proxy / writer endpoint\nwrite → Primary" as Proxy
 }
 rectangle "Основной регион" as RegionA {
   rectangle "AZ-A" as AZA {
     database "PostgreSQL\nPrimary" as Primary
   }
   rectangle "AZ-B" as AZB {
     database "PostgreSQL\nSync standby" as SyncReplica
   }
   component "Failover controller\nDCS quorum + fencing" as Controller
 }
 rectangle "DR-регион" as RegionB {
   database "PostgreSQL\nAsync standby" as DRReplica
 }
 cloud "Изолированный backup storage\nencrypted snapshots + WAL/PITR" as Backup

 App --> Proxy : SQL connection
 Proxy --> Primary : writes + read-after-write
 Primary --> SyncReplica : WAL / synchronous ACK\ncommit после flush standby
 Primary --> DRReplica : WAL / async\nRPO budget ≤ 5 min
 Primary --> Backup : snapshots + WAL archive
 SyncReplica --> Backup : recovery source (опц.)
 Controller --> Primary : health / leader state
 Controller --> SyncReplica : promote после fencing\n
 Controller ..> Proxy : обновить writer endpoint

 note bottom of SyncReplica
   Потеря одной AZ:
   автоматический failover;
   цель RTO ≤ 3 мин, RPO ≈ 0
 end note

 note bottom of DRReplica
   Потеря региона:
   promote только после fencing
   старого региона и запуска DR runbook.
   Асинхронная репликация не обещает RPO = 0.
 end note

 note right of Proxy
   Критические операции Saga
   читают актуальное состояние
   с Primary, не с read replica.
 end note
@enduml